description:
Rules that let several agents build in parallel without collisions:
- one beads task = one worktrunk branch = one portless URL;
- claim with bd update --claim;
- touch only the files your task owns;
- contracts in core/src/contracts change only through a dedicated task with a CONTRACTS.md changelog entry;
- the definition of done is check green + acceptance met + NOTES entry;
- no commits to other branches; no bd export outside master.
Include how to run, test and view a branch, and the reporting format back to the orchestrator.
Owns: elkdraw/AGENTS.md, elkdraw/NOTES.md, elkdraw/CONTRACTS.md changelog section.
Parallel: with P0.6, P0.9, P0.10. Blocked by P0.2, P0.3.

Collect the ground truth for later phases in test/fixtures/:
- the two dogfood final scenes (canvas/.artifacts/dogfood/*.excalidraw), each with a defects.json manifest listing every defect the testers reported (canvas/docs/dogfood-excalidraw-*.md), by element ids and the lint rule that should flag it;
- clean regions marked for the no-false-positive check;
- the ride-hailing and BST tasks as .mmd;
- a small Mermaid sample corpus per family we plan to support (flowchart, class, ER, state, requirement, sequence, gantt, timeline, mindmap, kanban), taken from Mermaid's docs with licence noted.
Owns: elkdraw/test/fixtures/**.
Parallel: with P0.2, P0.4, P0.11. Blocked by P0.1. Blocks P0.9.
